prusa-slicer (2.9.4+pm7m-0ppa3~resolute2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Rename binary package from "prusaslicer" to "prusa-slicer" to match
    the upstream Ubuntu/Debian package name (Replaces/Conflicts the old
    "prusaslicer" name; same name as upstream means apt picks our higher
    +pm7m version automatically over upstream 2.9.4+dfsg-N)
  * Drop boost::system from required Boost components
    (Ubuntu 26.04 ships Boost 1.90 without a boost_system CMake
    config; Boost.System has been header-only since 1.69)
  * Add explicit Build-Depends on Boost atomic, chrono, date-time
    components (now required by CMake 4.2 + Boost 1.90 modular
    BoostConfig.cmake — previously satisfied transitively)
  * Pass -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 (CMake 4.x dropped
    support for cmake_minimum_required below 3.5, which the
    bundled FindOpenVDB.cmake module still uses)
  * Bump OpenCASCADE pin to 7.9.2 (resolute ships OCCT 7.9.2;
    OCCT's version check requires exact MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH match)
  * Explicitly include <boost/asio/deadline_timer.hpp> in
    Bonjour.cpp and Serial.cpp (Boost 1.90 no longer pulls it
    in transitively from <boost/asio.hpp>)

 -- Sergey Kovrov <kovrov@gmail.com>  Tue, 28 Apr 2026 12:00:00 +0000

